# A fatal Node error (V8 out-of-memory, failed allocation, internal assertion) terminates the
# process via abort(), which Windows reports only as exit code 3221226505 / 0xC0000409 — a
# number that names neither the cause nor the file. These flags make Node dump a diagnostic
# report instead: the exact trigger, heap statistics and OS memory state at the moment it died.
#
# npm applies node-options to NODE_OPTIONS for every script in this project, so it covers both
# `npm run server` and `npm run client` without cross-env or any new dependency. Reports are
# written ONLY on a fatal error — a successful run costs nothing. The flip side is that this
# also covers `npm install`, `npm run build` and `npm test`, so .diagnostics/ may occasionally
# collect a report from something unrelated to the crash you are chasing.
node-options=--report-on-fatalerror --report-directory=.diagnostics
